NEARS-596 QA — residual gap (pre-existing, NOT introduced by this change)
Subcategory (childes) fetch failure on a fresh-category open while offline still
leaves the right-hand grid on an ENDLESS SHIMMER (the NearsErrorRetry fix does
NOT cover this path — it only covers the items fetch, offset==1).

Repro (emulator-5554, backend 8000 down, network interface UP):
  Categories tab (rail loaded) -> backend down -> tap a FRESH rail category
  (e.g. "Dairy & Eggs", never opened this session).

Why: CategoryController.getSubCategoryList() fetches /categories/childes/<id>
FIRST; only if that succeeds does it call getCategoryItemList(). The childes
fetch is NOT locally cached (CategoryRepository._getSubCategoryList hits the
network every time), so offline it returns null -> getCategoryItemList is never
called -> _itemFetchFailed stays false -> _productGrid renders the shimmer, not
NearsErrorRetry.

Observed log (childes fails; NO categories/items request follows):
  [FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/categories/childes/6 http_status=null type=ApiFailure msg="api request threw" correlation_id=08351b99-b677-4247-865b-8ef838335b35

Screenshot: gap-freshcategory-offline-shimmer.png (grid area = blank shimmer).

Scope note: The fix's stated scope is the ITEMS fetch (getCategoryItemList /
getOfferItemList), demonstrated working live for both paths. This childes-fetch
failure is a separate, pre-existing endless-shimmer path on the same screen and
is NOT a regression from commit 7e6800fe. Flagged so the PO can decide whether
to extend NEARS-596's scope (offline fresh-category open still hangs) or track
it as a follow-up.
